=20

Dear Administrative Court,

Further to your email requesting an ACO-compliant single-PDF bundle, I now =
resubmit the entire Judicial Review application in one consolidated document=
:

=20

Attachment: N461 Urgent Bundle =E2=80=93 28 November 2025 (single PDF)

=20

This document contains:
N461 Claim Form (with continuation sheets)
Detailed Statement of Facts
Detailed Grounds
Witness Statement and Exhibits
Draft Order
Signed medical evidence from my treating physician, Dr. Bruce Hayse
All supporting materials in the correct order
=20

I confirm that this is a single, unified, ACO-compliant PDF as requested.

1. Medical Emergency =E2=80=94 Urgent Judicial Action Required Today

=20

My treating physician, Dr Bruce Hayse, has submitted a signed clinical repo=
rt (included within the PDF bundle) confirming:
I am currently in a severe psychiatric crisis
My stability depends on timely judicial action
Any delay significantly increases the risk of hospitalisation
The matter must be treated as urgent for safeguarding reasons
=20

This places the Court under statutory duties engaged by:
Equality Act 2010, ss.20=E2=80=9321 (reasonable adjustments)
Equality Act 2010, s.149 (Public Sector Equality Duty)
The overriding objective, particularly protections for vulnerable litigants
Administrative Court disability guidance
=20

Given the seriousness of my condition, I respectfully request sealing and j=
udicial consideration today.

=20

Waiting until Monday would contradict the medical evidence and expose me to=
 significant and documented clinical risk.

=20

2. I am a litigant in person with no access to legal representation

=20

I respectfully reiterate that I cannot obtain legal advice due to financial=
 constraints.

Your request that I =E2=80=9Cseek legal advice=E2=80=9D cannot act as a barrier to my r=
ight to access the Administrative Court.

=20

I have now:
Complied fully with PD 54A
Provided the N461
Provided the N463
Filed every required continuation sheet
Assembled the bundle exactly as requested, in one coherent PDF
Served the Defendants
Provided urgent medical evidence
=20

3. Request for Immediate Action

=20

Given:
the medically urgent situation,
the ACO-compliant bundle now filed,
the fact that the N463 has been pending since 25 November,
and the statutory duties engaged,
=20

I respectfully request:

=20

(1) Sealing of the N461 today

=20

(2) Immediate referral of the N463 to a judge today

=20

(3) Confirmation of urgent listing

=20

I would be grateful for written confirmation of receipt, acceptance, and se=
aling.

=20

Thank you for your attention to this urgent and medically fragile matter.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

